{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.VhatPairCommutationTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.VhatPairCommutationTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.trace_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.trace_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vhat-pair-commutation-trace.lean#L44-L52","doc":"The trace consequence, stated parametrically.  Given any\n`R`-linear trace `tr` and any two elements that commute (which\nthey always do in a commutative ring), the trace is symmetric\nunder swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.VhatPairCommutationTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.VhatPairCommutationTrace","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vhat-pair-commutation-trace.lean#L25-L42","doc":"The pair commutation lemma at traced-volume level.\n\nFor any commutative ring `R` (instantiated in the QOU narrative\nas `ℤ[q^{±1/2}, z]`) and any two elements `V_i, V_j : R`, the\nproduct is symmetric: `V_i * V_j = V_j * V_i`.\n\nThis is the algebraic core of the lemma. The Markov-trace\nconsequence `tr_M (V_i V_j) = tr_M (V_j V_i) = z²` follows by\n`R`-linearity of `tr_M` and the pair Markov-trace identity\n`prop:markov-pair-z2`; we do not formalise the trace here\nbecause the underlying Hecke-algebra layer is in\n`QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovTrace` and is orthogonal to the lemma's\ncontent. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:vhat-pair-commutation-trace","label":"lem:vhat-pair-commutation-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vhat-pair-commutation-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}